## Icons

The 21 icons in `src/icon.rs` are this project's own SVG drawings of simple
geometric shapes (chevrons, a magnifier, a checkmark and similar). They are not
Apple's SF Symbols and contain none of Apple's artwork.

## Liquid Glass — the material of the floating layer

`src/glass.rs` draws Apple's Liquid Glass with a WGSL shader. Apple publishes no
implementation; the behaviour comes from its own description, and the shading,
the SDFs and the numbers are this crate's own. These were read for the approach
(no code was copied, and none of the projects' source is vendored):

| Project | Licence | Read for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [shuding/liquid-glass](https://github.com/shuding/liquid-glass) | MIT | The height field of a rounded rect turned into a surface normal, and the backdrop displaced by it — the approach this crate's lens follows, in a shader rather than an SVG filter |
| [rdev/liquid-glass-react](https://github.com/rdev/liquid-glass-react) | MIT | A refraction pass over a captured backdrop, with a specular edge on top |
| [archisvaze/liquid-glass](https://github.com/archisvaze/liquid-glass) | MIT | The split between the WebGL pass and a plain CSS blur where there is no GPU — this crate's fallback rule |
| [iyinchao/liquid-glass-studio](https://github.com/iyinchao/liquid-glass-studio) | MIT | Chromatic separation along the rim, and its order of magnitude (a pixel) |
| [samasante/liquid-glass](https://github.com/samasante/liquid-glass) | MIT | Sampling a live DOM backdrop, and where that costs redraws |
| [DnV1eX/LiquidGlassKit](https://github.com/DnV1eX/LiquidGlassKit) | MIT | The feature list a backport must keep (refraction, chromatic dispersion, Fresnel-style edge light, a glare that follows the surface's normals), and `LiquidLensView.swift`'s resting pill that lifts under a press |
| [Kyant0/AndroidLiquidGlass](https://github.com/Kyant0/AndroidLiquidGlass) | Apache-2.0 | Backdrop sampling in a Compose renderer, the variant split (regular/clear) of the same material, and the floating capsule tabs of `LiquidBottomTabs.kt` |
| [sdegenaar/liquid_glass_widgets](https://github.com/sdegenaar/liquid_glass_widgets) | MIT | Merging neighbouring shapes into one material (`GlassGroup`'s smooth union); the iOS 27 calibrated presets (`lib/theme/glass_theme_settings.dart`: glass colour, saturation, blur, frost, thickness, n = 1.24, paraxial lens, light angle, rim shade/light, body shade, shadow), the iOS 26 presets; the floating tab bar's geometry and placements (`lib/widgets/surfaces/glass_tab_bar.dart`); the minimise state machine and its thresholds (`lib/widgets/surfaces/shared/tab_bar_minimize_controller.dart`); the graduated blur (`docs/PROGRESSIVE_BLUR.md`); the rim light's lobe shape and magnitudes (`shaders/liquid_glass_render.frag`, `shaders/render.glsl`); and the native-vs-implementation stills `docs/assets/ios27_parity_light.png` / `ios27_parity_dark.png` used as the visual target |
| [whynotmake-it/flutter_liquid_glass](https://github.com/whynotmake-it/flutter_liquid_glass) | Apache-2.0 | Shape and container APIs for a glass widget set |
| [conorluddy/LiquidGlassReference](https://github.com/conorluddy/LiquidGlassReference) | none | The written specification of the feature set: lensing against blur, specular response, variants, containers |

Apple's own sources, used as the specification and as acceptance criteria:
[Meet Liquid Glass](https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/219/),
HIG [Materials](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/materials)
[Tab bars](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/tab-bars),
[Adopting Liquid Glass](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/technologyoverviews/adopting-liquid-glass),
